CodeBrix patch 0006 - backport of upstream #602: WGPU_WHOLE_MAP_SIZE in wgpuBufferMapAsync
(wgpu-native/src/lib.rs)

WHAT: wgpuBufferMapAsync passes None (map from offset to the end of the buffer) for
size == WGPU_WHOLE_MAP_SIZE instead of the sentinel as a literal size (a validation error).
UPSTREAM: gfx-rs/wgpu-native PR #602 "fix `WGPU_WHOLE_MAP_SIZE` case in `bufferMapAsync`" by
@Vipitis, merged 2026-06-29 as d84d8acde2848c9af9ac4b9ac7455d0294da0e7e - after the v29.0.1.1 tag,
so not in the vendored release. This is that PR's src/lib.rs hunk unchanged (its CHANGELOG.md hunk
is not carried); drop this patch when the vendored release contains it.

--- a/wgpu-native/src/lib.rs
+++ b/wgpu-native/src/lib.rs
@@ -1152,7 +1152,10 @@ pub unsafe extern "C" fn wgpuBufferMapAsync(
     if let Err(cause) = context.buffer_map_async(
         buffer_id,
         offset as wgt::BufferAddress,
-        Some(size as wgt::BufferAddress),
+        match size {
+            conv::WGPU_WHOLE_MAP_SIZE => None,
+            _ => Some(size as wgt::BufferAddress),
+        },
         operation,
     ) {
         handle_error(error_sink, cause, None, "wgpuBufferMapAsync");
